  "summary": "My technical journey begins as a teannager who's Mother was pushing the boundaries for women in a technical field. When I was a teanager, she brought home a piece of equipment that looked like an oversized laptop (which didn't exist at that time) with a green screen and the first version of the game 'Pong'.  I visited her work several times as my curiosity grew in her role as a Manager, leading the department that built these huge hard disks (so Old, even Google couldn't find me a picture).  \n\nThroughout my education, I was the student who sat near the front and asked lots of questions. My instructors would glance at me to see if my forehead was scrunched in a look of puzzlement. If it did, they knew others in the class must have the same confusion. I often heard from my classmates that they didn't have to ask the questions because they knew I would.  My passion to learn and push the status quo has served me well in my personal life and my career.\n\nWith over 28 years of development experience in the healthcare industry, I'm working with a group of very smart people to build the next generation of Healthcare, driven by AI on the Oracle OCI platform. Join us if you share the same passion. \nhttps://www.oracle.com/careers/",
